  "question": {
    "text": "Let [x]&nbsp;denote the greatest integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>. Consider the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then the value of the integral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math> is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FRLBC",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
